When writing OpenCL kernels, prioritize Integer math and Bit-shifting over floating point.
Ensure all memory buffers are aligned for high-performance GPU access.

## Agent workflow (project)

- Do not create new source or header files unless the user explicitly asks for a new file or names a path to create.
- Prefer edits inside existing files; consolidate helpers into an existing translation unit when reasonable.
- utilize previous written code to inspire new code format, variable name, comments, function structure.
- ask user for feedback on major decisions with question prompts.
- keep change minimal without profoundly changing code flow/structure without being otherwise requested
- Do not add standalone markdown documentation unless requested.
- comments should not end with period "."